---
/**
 * `/learn` has no landing of its own.
 *
 * The rail lists the Learn surfaces directly, so a page here would be a menu
 * duplicating a menu. But the URL is guessable and typed, and a 404 on it would
 * read as "Learn is broken" — so it sends you to Knowledge, the surface you
 * reach for most.
 *
 * Static output means this is a client-side redirect rather than a 302.
 */
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/learn/knowledge" />
  <link rel="canonical" href="/learn/knowledge" />
  <title>Learn — Cadence</title>
</head>
<body>
  <p><a href="/learn/knowledge">Continue to Knowledge</a></p>
  <script>window.location.replace('/learn/knowledge');</script>
</body>
</html>
